ir. Currently I have two chows: [B3,B4,B5] and implicitly, the W3 kong could be seen as part of a chow-type hand, but kongs don't count as chows. Wait: **All Chows** requires four chows and a pair. My W3 kong is actually a concealed kong formed via BuGang after Peng, so it originated as a pung from discard \u2014 not a chow. So not eligible.\n\nWait: **Melded Hand** (6 points): all melds and pair completed using opponent's tiles. My W3 kong and W4 pung were formed via Peng/BuGang (exposed), and B3-B5 was Chi (using previous player's discard). So all melds are exposed and formed via other players\u2019 discards. Only thing missing is the winning tile: if I win by claiming a discard for the pair, then Melded Hand qualifies.\n\nAlso, Seat Wind = South (F2), Prevalent Wind = South. I have no F2 pung. But I do have W4 pung, W3 kong \u2014 both Characters. No wind/dragon melds.\n\nBut I discarded F2 earlier. Someone else Peng\u2019d it. So no chance.\n\nSo possible patterns:\n- **All Pungs**? No \u2014 I have a chow.\n- **All Chows**? I have one chow and two pungs/kongs \u2192 no.\n- Best bet: try to complete **Chicken Hand** (8 points minimum required). Need at least 8 points.\n\nLet\u2019s assess possible patterns I can reach:\n- I could draw or catch a tile to make a pair. Current hand: five singles.\n- If I keep J2, and get another J2, I get a pair. Then Dragon Pung (if I Peng) \u2192 2 points. Plus Melded Hand (6) \u2192 total 8 \u2192 valid.\n- Alternatively, if I form a pair like W6+W6, and win by stealing discard, still Melded Hand (6), plus maybe One Voided Suit? I have W and B and J \u2192 three suits and honor \u2192 not one voided suit.\n- One Voided Suit: having only two suits \u2192 I have W and B \u2192 two suits, plus honor \u2192 counts as three types \u2192 no.\n- No Honors? I have J2 \u2192 invalid.\n- All Simples? W6, W8, W9 are not simple (W6 yes, W8 yes, W9 no \u2192 terminal). So W9 breaks it.\n\nSo safest path: **Melded Hand (6)** + **Dragon Pung (